1826	{"artifactId":"TASK-dae67bfc7da310cc-s1-t1","entry":{"id":"00mwjbhvtn001-7264b073-f647-4ff3-a15b-c6d2e35f303d","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-16T13:46:52.379Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"fail","summary":"The new review-retirement-endpoints.test.ts passes and the four acceptance checks hold for the new frozen paths, but the Task leaves a real regression unaddressed: src/daemon/steps/host.ts now unconditionally short-circuits any call named 'insrc_review_step' or 'insrc_code_review_step' inside createStepCallHandler, before even looking at the tool table — this bypasses test-supplied custom handlers too. Pre-existing, untouched test files src/mcp/__tests__/design-review.test.ts and src/mcp/__tests__/task-review.test.ts build a `stepToolTable({tools:{insrc_review_step/insrc_code_review_step: handleDesignReviewStep/handleTaskReviewStep}})` and drive it through `createStepCallHandler`, then assert a working review flow (e.g. `assert.equal(ack.status,'pending')`, assignment/progress/publish behavior). Those assertions can no longer be satisfied since every call to those two tool names now always throws the rewrite error regardless of the table passed in — the full sweep (`npx tsx --test 'src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts'`) would fail on those files. The daemon's validate run only exercised the one new test file named for this Task, so it didn't surface this; nothing in t1/t3's stated scope says these legacy functional test files are deferred for deletion (t3 only covers runtime wiring: workers/owners/progress producers), so this is an unaddressed regression outside — and caused by — this Task's own change, not scope the Task called for leaving broken.","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
1235	{"artifactId":"TASK-dae67bfc7da310cc-s1-t1","entry":{"id":"00mwjbmbg9002-f8e02fa9-3089-4a93-8a9b-c1614e12b6fa","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-16T13:50:19.257Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"All four acceptance checks are objectively satisfied against the real code: the 25 IPC methods and 2 MCP tools remain registered with their original frozen schemas/phases, every call routes to the same stateless reviewUnavailable() error with no dependency access, workflow.reviewDecision/team/artifact endpoints are untouched, and the step host now short-circuits review-step dispatch before any ownership allocation. Daemon-run typecheck and the two required integration tests (verified to exercise what their names claim) both passed. Changed files are confined to the review-retirement surface (MCP schemas/handlers, daemon RPC shims, step host/handlers, router's review-owner path, workflow/review-unavailable + its test) plus the new test file — consistent with the Task's stated scope, with orphan ownership-infra deletion explicitly deferred to t3 as the Task specifies.","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
